00:00:03,050 --> 00:00:07,871
Biomimicry is the human practice of learning from and imitating things found in nature

3
00:00:07,871 --> 00:00:10,080
in order to create new inventions.

4
00:00:10,080 --> 00:00:17,110
This way, scientists and engineers can create innovative solutions that are both efficient and sustainable.

5
00:00:17,110 --> 00:00:24,372
One well-known example of biomimicry is the development of a widely used fastening system.The

6
00:00:24,372 --> 00:00:30,090
inventor was inspired by the way burrs, uh thorns, from plants stuck to his dog’s fur.

7
00:00:30,090 --> 00:00:34,489
By replicating the tiny hooks found on the burrs he removed from the dog

8
00:00:34,489 --> 00:00:37,180
fur, he created the new fastening system.

9
00:00:37,180 --> 00:00:42,949
Another example is the design of energy-efficient buildings based on the ventilation system of

10
